gest utility, pulled its C$2.4B offering on 14 October.\n- **Pellham is changing its plans to match.** It said it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. A utility that was confident it could raise equity wouldn't do that. The equity shortfall is already forcing capex down.\n- **The plans were filed before the pulled offering.** Pellham and Norvane Utilities filed their 2027 capital plans in October, mostly for substations and transformers. The filed amounts probably overstate what will actually be spent, at least for Pellham.\n- **What I couldn't see.** I don't have Norvane's own funding position or the dollar size of the 2027 plans. Those are in the utility tender calendar and Pellham's market statement, which I didn't read.\n\n**What this means for the other nodes:** expect 2027 grid-equipment demand from Pellham to come in lower, and treat equity as an unreliable source. The `utility_spreads` series is the place to check whether debt can fill the gap. That question belongs to nodes n3 and n5.","ttft_ms":3505,"type":"result","duration_ms":28382,"uuid":"2e85bbca-0423-49e1-b521-b6c24ce3bf5c","ttft_stream_ms":2639,"time_to_request_ms":76,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":26,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":66,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":133,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss_mib":223,"process_cpu_ms_turn":621,"pro